// The LIVE /backends sign-in screens, as the compiled admin renders them (outerHTML of .admin-login), captured read-only on
// 2026-11-12 by a Playwright job on the VPS (sporta-probe-login2, playwright:v1.49.0-noble) against https://www.sporta.com.kw/backends
// with every /api/ call answered INSIDE the browser (me -> null, or 202 need_password_change; login -> 202 need_code;
// google_available -> false), so no sign-in attempt reached the server and no lock or rate limit was touched. Build:
// /assets/index-BtzlNXGI.js + AdminApp-vmvSQvXS.js + AdminApp-Dw3t3z9Z.css. Do not edit by hand; re-capture if the build changes.
//
// The live build has NO device-passcode screen (no "passcode" string in AdminApp-vmvSQvXS.js); the passcode quick unlock exists
// only in this repo's own admin (src/admin/AdminApp.jsx), which is not what serves /backends. The reset-link step ("Choose a new
// password", reached from the e-mailed link) uses the same classes as the forced change below (admin-login__recovery-panel, two
// new-password fields with reveal buttons, the checklist, an orange submit) and is covered by it.
//
// Live measurements of the same capture (Chromium, isMobile, html dir=rtl lang=ar, theme light), for the record:
//   390x844  sign-in: card 366x596 at y=124 floating in grey; fields 16px, 50px; Show 64x44 (13px); Forgot 119x44; submit 48px.
//   320x568  sign-in: page 660px tall (form panel min-height 600px); forced change 855px; code step 635px.
//   844x390  (phone landscape) sign-in: card 524x668, page 709px tall for a 390px screen: the form panel keeps min-height 600px.
//   1280x860 sign-in: split card 1077x622, brand panel 564px wide.
//   Every input already computes to 16px (no iOS focus zoom) and every button is 44px or more.

export const BUILD = { index: '/assets/index-BtzlNXGI.js', js: 'AdminApp-vmvSQvXS.js', css: 'AdminApp-Dw3t3z9Z.css', captured: '2026-11-12' }

